<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Justicialist Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">founded <a href="/years/1946">1946</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Partido Justicialista, PJ, Peronist Party, Partido Peronista</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Justicialist Party, also known as the Peronist Party, is a major political party in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> and the largest branch within <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peronism">Peronism</a>. It was founded in 1946 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-peron">Juan Perón</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eva-peron">Eva Perón</a>, uniting the three parties that had supported Perón in the election. Its most consistent base of support has been the General Confederation of Labor, Argentina's largest trade union. All Peronist entities were banned from elections after Perón was overthrown in 1955, until his return to Argentina in 1973. Aside from Juan Perón, eleven presidents of Argentina have belonged to the party, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlos-menem">Carlos Menem</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nestor-kirchner">Néstor Kirchner</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cristina-fernandez-de-kirchner">Cristina Fernández de Kirchner</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The &quot;Peronist March&quot;, officially &quot;Los muchachos peronistas&quot; (&quot;The Peronist Boys&quot;), is the anthem of the Peronist movement founded and led by Juan Domingo Perón and the official song of Argentina's <b>Justicialist Party</b>.</blockquote><a href="/songs/peronist-march">Peronist March</a></li></ul></section>
